Now, each truck can carry 2000 pounds. So, to find out how many trucks are needed, I need to divide the total weight by the capacity of one truck. That would be 6000 divided by 2000. Let me do that division. 6000 divided by 2000 is 3. So, 3 trucks are needed. Wait, but sometimes when these problems have remainders, you need to round up because you can't have a fraction of a truck. But in this case, 6000 divided by 2000 is exactly 3, so no rounding needed. Therefore, the answer should be 3 trucks.
